<p>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>

<table align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="80%">
			
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB"><h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;Who are the Armigers of Mirth?</h3></td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">
			The Armigers of Mirth is a guild comprised of avid MMORPG game fans, initially formed in
			EverQuest<sup>©</sup>, which has since expanded into some other games, including
			Dark Age of Camelot<sup>©</sup>.<p>
			Some of us were ready to try some new MMORPGs, a few still play EQ<sup>©</sup>, but we
			all share the love of online games and envision the Armigers as becoming
			a general guild for various MMORPGs.<p>
			In EQ<sup>©</sup> our common bond was lots of virtual drinking, brewing, and merry making - we hope to be able to
			carry on a similiar tradition in Dark Age of Camelot<sup>©</sup>. 
			You can read more in our Charter <a class="BaseC" href="GuildCharter.asp" target="_self"><b>here</b></a><p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">
				<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;What does &quot;Armigers of Mirth&quot; mean?</h3>
			</td>
		</tr>	
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">			
			<i>Armigers</i> comes from the Latin word meaning &quot;arms bearer&quot;, while <i>Mirth</i> comes from the
			old or middle English word meaning &quot;merriment and cheerfulness, often accompanied with laughter&quot;. 
			That tells you a lot about who we are...<p>
			</td>
		</tr>	
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">
				<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;So what do you do?</h3>
			</td>
		</tr>	
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">
			Basically we enjoy playing onlines games with real life and online friends in
			a fun and co-operative setting. While games like Dark Age of Camelot<sup>©</sup> have a PvP (Player vs. Player) or RvR (Realm vs. Realm) element
			that may set us up 'against' one another - we are a circle of friends who like sharing game information,
			helping our guild mates out, exploring the worlds we play in, and having an all-around good time.<p>
			</td>
		</tr>	
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">
				<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;Whose side are you on in Dark Age of Camelot<sup>©</sup>?</h3>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">				
			Any. We don't exclude membership based on online persona... we play any profession, race and in any
			Realm. Our only allegiance per se, is to having good guildmates - people who
			play fairly and honestly, behave respectfully towards other players, and don't do anything that
			would give the Guild or its members a bad reputation.<p> 
			</td>
		</tr>				
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">
				<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;Where Realms & Servers do you play in Dark Age of Camelot<sup>©</sup>?</h3>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">				
			Since we have an interest in exploring all the taverns... er... realms in DAoC<sup>©</sup>, we can be found on several servers.
			<ul>
			<li><i>Hibernia</i> Armigers mainly play on <i>Percival</i></li>
			<li><i>Albion</i> Armigers mainly play on <i>Galahad</i></li>
			<li><i>Midgard</i> Armigers mainly play on <i>Morgan Le Fay</i></li>			
			<li>We have also recently established ourselves on the <i>Gaheris</i> cross-realm co-op server</li>	
			</ul>
			You can also see who plays where on the <a href="CharactersView.asp" class="BaseC" target="_self"><b>characters list</b></a> page.<p>
			</td>
		</tr>	
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">
				<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;So How Can I Join?</h3>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td Class="MainB">				
			<a  class="BaseC" href="GuildJoining.asp" target="_self"><b>Click Here</b></a> to learn more about joining the Armigers of Mirth<p>
			</td>
		</tr>

			
